From e197a270bc10971d3af667fc9175db3006529ca2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:41:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Kanban sync heal: keep parks, guard live claims,
 sync the heal's run

Follow-ups from the PR1341 exact-head review (GitHub review 5872637434):

- _stale_lifecycle: a live claim_lock is a local worker holding the card,
  so a terminal replica on the same run is never adopted over it.
- heal_running_over_ended_run: a run that ended blocked, review_requested
  or scheduled puts the card back in that park (blocked/review/scheduled)
  instead of todo, when the park's own event is the card's last lifecycle
  move. A dependency block, a later unblock/wake/reopen, or a missing park
  event still lands todo as before.
- The once-per-run gate now logs a warning when it skips a card.
- status_healed carries the run as the event's run_id column (synced as
  run_uid) instead of a local id in the payload; the gate reads both.
- Committed negative tests: a held claim_lock and a held lease keep the card
  running over an ended run.
